{
  "requirement": "Before that commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to revert the drafts the user rejected or deferred and to list them in their report.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.commit.revert` says that, before the commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to revert the drafts the user rejected or deferred, and to list them in their report. The only clause is about what the skill's text tells agents to do. It prescribes no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or named interface. It says nothing about how the skill is built, such as which section or file layout the directive must live in. Any wording or placement in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` that gives the same directions would satisfy it, so the obligation is purely about observable content and not structure. The skill file is already linked to the requirement as an implementation root (`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, via an Implements edge). So no structural obligation needs further implementation evidence, and no marker is missing. Whether the skill text really contains the directive is a behavioral question, left to the behavioral criterion.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one observable obligation. Before the commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to revert drafts the user rejected or deferred, and to list them in their report.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reverts_rejected_and_deferred_drafts_before_committing]` covers it. It does the following:\n- It locates the commit step with `step_of(\"habeas-requirements\", \"all groups together\")`.\n- It takes that step's text, with whitespace collapsed, through `step` and `workflow_steps`.\n- It calls `assert_text_in_order` with two phrases. The first is \"Revert drafts the user rejected or deferred (`git restore -p`) and list them in your report\". The second is \"then commit it\".\n\nThe first phrase covers both the revert direction and the report-listing direction. The second phrase must appear after the first, so the test also covers the \"before that commit\" ordering. Removing either direction, or moving the revert after the commit, would make the assertion panic. The skill text in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` (Workflow, step 5) matches these phrases.\n\nNo other behavioral obligation or boundary case needs a test.",
  "references": "9eb15ef719e9102dc5daf951360c2a28960ead1b16fffbd7549b6d609923a19f",
